--
N5008 [class.default.ctor]/2: a defaulted default constructor whose
member or base has no default constructor is defined as DELETED;
/4 + [dcl.fct.def.delete]/2: that is an error only when the deleted
definition is odr-USED.  Nothing here odr-uses them.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept silently.  The deleted-implicit-member recovery in
convert_function (round 98) already handles this shape on the current
tree -- the cvise fleet's frozen reference binary predated it, so the
artifact arrived as a would-be KNOWNBUG and was flipped to CORE on
harvest after test.pl passed (1 assertion, non-vacuous).  Kept as the
minimal regression test for that recovery; the residual cosmetic issue
(the recovered errors' TEXT still leaks to stderr) is tracked in the
findings notes.
Reduced by cvise (fleet /tmp/cv98, 99,167-line goto-symex dog-food
carrier from src/goto-symex/goto_state.h) to 11 lines.
